{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Words of</b>. Among the words of the ancients are some that are like goads to a beast, chastising and sharpening the soul, and there are like great planted nails that hold the doors so they do not come apart, and this is the instruction of man. Some say, \"and like nails planted\" — the words of the compiler of collections are those who gather from many books and compose compositions; even though they all differ, one Creator taught them all." "<b>And the word shepherd</b>. Because he likened man to a beast that requires goads."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Resolved 'בעל אסופות' as 'the compiler of collections'; the phrase is ambiguous and could alternatively refer to a specific title or work."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:23.383167257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}